# LeakSanitizer suppressions for `scripts/check.sh asan`: the tests that leak
# on purpose. Each one hands an API `'static` data made at run time
# (`Box::leak`), or forgets a value a thread it starts still names
# (`mem::forget`). A leak whose stack holds none of these functions fails the
# run. Add a line only for a leak a test makes itself, never for one in the
# crates.
leak:a_refused_zero_copy_send_is_sent_again_with_a_copy
leak:large_writes_arrive_intact_with_or_without_zero_copy
leak:a_peer_that_breaks_the_ring_is_reported_not_followed
leak:a_peer_that_closes_its_socket_mid_channel_is_gone_after_its_messages
leak:an_argument_written_in_pieces_or_not_at_all_is_one_argument
leak:tls12_with_record_limit
